  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Harvest quantities can be posted on a board, and neighbors can state when they can collect.\", \"decision\": \"How should harvest offers be matched to available collectors?\", \"goal\": \"Keep routine garden work visible and shared without requiring everyone to attend at the same time.\", \"problem\": \"A small community garden has established beds, safe shared tools, a water supply, and volunteers whose availability varies. Gardening methods are already agreed; the new work is organizing participation, observations, and shared resources. Each decision below covers a distinct coordination need and can be combined with any choices at the other decisions.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nNeighbors state collection times before garden volunteers divide harvest quantities among those times. Harvest portions are arranged around actual collection availability.\nGarden volunteers and neighbors agree on quantities and collection times together on the board. Each offer is paired immediately with a collection plan.\nGarden volunteers post harvest quantities before neighbors choose collection times. Collection plans respond to a known available harvest."
    }
  ],
